    "introduction": "Born in the United Kingdom and raised on the numerous film sets that his father Alan Marshall produced, Marshall grew up observing and learning from the ever-evolving world of filmmaking. Marshall quickly climbed the ranks as a First Assistant Director and successfully completed multiple projects working for award winning directors including Martin Campbell, Antoine Fuqua, John Woo, Adrian Lyne, Terry Gilliam, Catherine Hardwicke, Tarsem, Scott Cooper, Gavin O'Connor, Jonathan Nolan, Elizabeth Chai Vasarhelyi, and Jimmy Chin. Taking advantage of his experience as a First Assistant Director, Marshall began to get involved as a Producer on various projects, including Twilight, Warrior, Immortals, Snow White, Out of the Furnace, Miss Bala, The In Between, Rosaline , The Foreigner (PGA), Den of Thieves, NYAD and Lionsgate's 2024 release \"Dirty Angels.\" In 2011 Marshall made his transition to directing and helmed 2nd Unit on Antoine Fuqua's action film Olympus Has Fallen and then went on to direct action units on numerous feature films for directors, Martin Campbell, Catherine Hardwicke, Gavin Oconnor, Kenya Barris, Christian Gudeghast. In 2023/4 Jamie directed the feature film Copperhead - an action / thriller for Voltage staring Lucien Laviscount, Hannah John Kamen, Lewis Tan and Holt McCallany.",
